<BaseLayout title="ST36 (Zusanli) — Leg Three Miles Point" description="Learn how to locate and stimulate ST36 (Zusanli) — the Leg Three Miles point. Benefits include digestive health, energy boost, and immune support." articleSchema={true}>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 lg:px-6">
    <h1 class="mb-4">ST36 (Zusanli) — Leg Three Miles</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-lg mb-8">ST36, known as Zusanli or Leg Three Miles, is a major acupressure point for digestive health, energy, and longevity. It is one of the most commonly used points in both acupuncture and acupressure traditions.</p>

    <section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Location</h2>
    <img src="/images/st36-location.png" alt="ST36 acupressure point location on the lower leg" class="w-full max-w-sm mx-auto rounded-xl shadow-sm" />
    <p class="mb-3">ST36 is located on the lower leg, approximately 4 cun (about four finger-widths) below the bottom of the kneecap, one finger-width lateral (toward the outside) from the shinbone (tibia). It lies on the Stomach meridian.</p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Benefits &amp; Uses</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li><strong>Digestive health:</strong> ST36 regulates the entire digestive system ?it is used for bloating, indigestion, nausea, and poor appetite.</li>
      <li><strong>Energy and vitality:</strong> Known as a Qi-building point, it helps combat fatigue and general weakness.</li>
      <li><strong>Immune support:</strong> Regular stimulation strengthens the immune system and increases resistance to illness.</li>
      <li><strong>Longevity:</strong> In traditional Chinese medicine, ST36 is considered a longevity point that supports overall health and vitality.</li>
      <li><strong>Leg strength:</strong> It improves circulation in the lower limbs and may help with knee pain and weakness.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">How to Massage ST36</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Sit with your knee bent and foot flat on the floor.</li>
      <li>Place your thumbs on ST36 points on both legs.</li>
      <li>Apply firm pressure using a circular kneading motion or steady push.</li>
      <li>Hold for 1— minutes per leg, breathing deeply.</li>
      <li>Repeat daily for best results.</li>
    </ol>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Science &amp; Research</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">A 2020 meta-analysis in <em>Medicine</em> found that ST36 acupressure improved gastrointestinal function in post-operative patients and reduced nausea.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33031396/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1</a></sup> Research in <em>Journal of Neurogastroenterology and Motility</em> showed that ST36 stimulation increased gastric motility and vagal activity.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27156346/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">2</a></sup></p>
    <p class="mb-3">A study in <em>Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine</em> demonstrated that ST36 acupressure enhanced natural killer cell activity, supporting the immune-boosting claims of traditional use.<sup><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24693282/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3</a></sup></p>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Precautions</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-1 text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <li>Do not massage directly over a bruise, wound, or infection on the lower leg.</li>
      <li>Avoid deep pressure if you have varicose veins in the area.</li>
      <li>Use gentle pressure on the elderly or those with fragile bones.</li>
      <li>Discontinue if you experience discomfort or unusual pain.</li>
    </ul>

    </section><section class="mb-8"><h2 class="mb-4">Related Points</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">ST36 works well with <a href="/points/cv6-qihai-acupressure-point">CV6 (Qihai)</a> for Qi deficiency and fatigue. For digestive issues, combine with <a href="/points/sp6-sanyinjiao-acupressure-point">SP6 (Sanyinjiao)</a> and <a href="/points/li4-hegu-acupressure-point">LI4 (Hegu)</a>.</p>
  </section></article>
